# Deletion counts follow rediscovered aliases

A staged checkout counts every discovered session alias, even when the query
hides those aliases. Rediscovery must replace these counts rather than accumulate
old entries.

Create a named workspace with two live sessions pointing to its checkout. The
second session needs direct tmux setup because CLI creation would reuse the
existing session. CLI creation prints `alpha/feature`, which is then renamed to
`first`. Filter to `first` so only one alias is visible among five discovered
rows: two aliases, the default repository, the runner, and the UI session.

    :b jj tmux cat (available)
    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ -q jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --base alpha --create feature (exit: 0)

```stdout
alpha/feature
```

    :t rename-session -t alpha/feature first (success)
    :t new-session -d -s second -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=second:' @smth.repo '#{pane_start_path}' (success)
    :t new-session -d -s ui "smth -r 'alpha*'; cat" (success)
    :t resize-window -t ui:0 -x 120 -y 14 (success)
    :p ui:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k C-p first
    :settle -e '1/5' -e C-d (settled)

Stage the shared checkout. Both aliases count, but only `first` is visible.

    :k C-d
    :snap -e '2 sessions' -e '1 hidden'

```terminal
session: first                                                                                                         ┃
  1/5 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                                              ┃
   first~1                                  ~/first                                                               repo ┃
   first~1                                                                                                        tmux ┃
▌× first                                    ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage, [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                 delete [C-y] 2 sessions (1 hidden) [C-g] cancel┃
```

Clear the query to show both aliases staged. The total stays at two, with no
hidden sessions.

    :k C-u
    :snap -e '5/5' -e '2 sessions'

```terminal
session:                                                                                                               ┃
  5/5 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                                              ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌■ ui                                                                                                                  ┃
 ■ runner                                                                                                              ┃
 × first                                    ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
 × second                                   ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
   alpha                                    ~/alpha                                                                    ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                                           delete [C-y] 2 sessions [C-g] cancel┃
```

Restore the query before the next flag toggle so it still targets `first`.

    :k first
    :settle -e '1/5' -e '1 hidden' (settled)

Add a third alias and toggle the selected session's flag to trigger discovery.
The count should grow to three, with two hidden aliases.

    :t new-session -d -s third -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=third:' @smth.repo '#{pane_start_path}' (success)
    :k C-f
    :snap -e '3 sessions' -e '2 hidden'

```terminal
session: first                                                                                                         ┃
  1/6 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                                              ┃
   first~1                                  ~/first                                                               repo ┃
   first~1                                                                                                        tmux ┃
▌× first                                    ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage, [C-x] close, [C-f] unflag                               delete [C-y] 3 sessions (2 hidden) [C-g] cancel┃
```

Clear the query again. All three aliases should carry staging markers, and none
should be counted as hidden.

    :k C-u
    :snap -e '6/6' -e '3 sessions'

```terminal
session:                                                                                                               ┃
  6/6 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                                              ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌■ ui                                                                                                                  ┃
 ■ runner                                                                                                              ┃
 × first                                    ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
 × second                                   ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
 × third                                    ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
   alpha                                    ~/alpha                                                                    ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                                           delete [C-y] 3 sessions [C-g] cancel┃
```

Restore the query so the next flag toggle targets the surviving `first` session.

    :k first
    :settle -e '1/6' -e '2 hidden' (settled)

Remove both hidden aliases and toggle the flag again. Rediscovery should count
only the surviving selected session and remove the hidden-count annotation.

    :t kill-session -t second (success)
    :t kill-session -t third (success)
    :k C-f
    :snap -e '1 session' -e '1/4'

```terminal
session: first                                                                                                         ┃
  1/4 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                                              ┃
   first~1                                  ~/first                                                               repo ┃
   first~1                                                                                                        tmux ┃
▌× first                                    ~/alpha.feature                                                            ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
 [C-d] unstage, [C-x] close, [C-f] flag                                             delete [C-y] 1 session [C-g] cancel┃
```

Clear the query one last time. Only `first` should remain staged; the removed
aliases should be absent from the full session list.

    :k C-u
    :snap -e '4/4' -e '1 session'

```terminal
session:                                                                                                               ┃
  4/4 | [C-s] ↑l ↑r ↓n | [C-r] repo: none                                                                              ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
